#
# Line-ending policy: everything in this repository is LF, in the working tree as well as in the
# index. Every tool the flow uses writes LF (Bender, Verible, PeakRDL, FlooGen, Padrick, and the
# generated Makefiles and TCL scripts), and so do the two reference SoCs this project is modelled
# on, so LF is the ecosystem's convention rather than a preference.
#
# Before this file existed the repository was mixed - 44 CRLF files against 83 LF, with no rule by
# directory or extension - because part of the sources had been authored through the now-obsolete
# Windows workflow. That mixture cost two accidental conversions, each inflating a hundred-line
# change into a two-thousand-line diff, and it required a manual check before rewriting any file
# from a script. Declaring the policy here removes the class of mistake instead of guarding
# against it: a checkout normalizes on the way in, so a file edited on a Windows host and
# committed back arrives as LF.
#
# 'text=auto' lets git detect text files, and 'eol=lf' fixes what it writes to the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf
